			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Morani looks a little confused for a moment and the impersonation drops. “I know of a recipe for MIND Worm steaks, it’s kinda tricky; almost as bad as patty melts. But if you got meat from the Shardwurms, the only thing I know of to do with it is pickle it. It pretty easy actually, the meat is quite firm so it holds up well to the seaweed vinegar and that strong taste softens a bit with the oyster sauce. Just put the three parts together in a spit, cook over a really low heat and your good to go. As for a wine to go with it, Hmmm…. A fish wine should go well with the oyster sauce… A honey mead would balance the vinegar; sweet and sour work well together… Dwarven ale is another one but that’s not a wine. OH, and if you want something very different try some root beer. It’s not alcoholic at all and it goes back to the sweet and sour taste…” Realizing that she’s babbling on, the Ranger blushes a little and shuts her mouth. 
